#%PAM-1.0
# phiOS — PAM service for phi-shell's own lock screen (S-34,
# phi-shell/Lock/Lock.qml's PamContext.config: "phi-shell-lock").
#
# NOT applied by this repository (I-09, master plan §5.5): shown by
# `phios-install --system-diff`, installed by the user with sudo, one file
# at a time, after reading the diff.
#
# Deliberately NOT PamContext's own default ("login"): that service is
# configured on Arch for the text-console `login` program and may carry
# modules (pam_securetty and similar) that assume a real controlling tty —
# a graphical lock screen invoked with no tty at all is exactly the case
# those modules exist to reject, which would fail every login attempt for
# a reason that has nothing to do with the password being correct. This
# mirrors the same minimal service every other Wayland lock screen on Arch
# ships for itself (swaylock, hyprlock): include the system's own
# already-correct authentication stack, nothing more.
auth            include         system-auth
account         include         system-auth
password        include         system-auth
session         include         system-auth
